    "title": "ICSE Steering Committee",
    "text": "ICSE Steering Committee\nICSE\nInternational Conference\non Software Engineering®\nHOME\nNews from the SC\nEDI STATEMENT\nCONDUCT & SAFETY\nHISTORY\nPROCEEDINGS\nINFLUENTIAL PAPERS\nORGANIZING ICSE\nSTEERING COMMITTEE\nICSE SC Documents\nSPONSORS\nCONTACTS\nLast updated\nJan 2026\nICSE STEERING COMMITTEE\nThe ICSE Steering Committee is responsible for constituting and guiding each\nedition of ICSE, the International Conference on Software Engineering® and for\nestablishing and evaluating practices that are binding upon the organizers of each\nconference for the continued technical and financial success of ICSE.\nACM and IEEE–CS are co-sponsors of the ICSE and ACM SIGSOFT and IEEE\nTCSE represent their respective software engineering societies in the organization of the\nICSE conference through their participation in the ICSE Steering Committee and through their\nreview and approval of the budget for each conference.\nTo update the icse-conferences.org website, please send a note to the\nicse-conferences.org webmaster.\nThe table below lists the current ICSE Steering Committee members. Last\nUpdated: May 2025\nName\nAffiliation\nMember Status\nRui Abreu\nUniversity of Porto, Portugal\nICSE 2024 GC\nMauricio Aniche\nAdyen\nICSE 2024 SEIP\nKelly Blincoe\nUniversity of Auckland, New Zealand\nRepresenting 2nd past ACM SIGSOFT Chair*\nJan Bosch\nChalmers University of Technology\nICSE 2028 SEIP\nLionel Briand\nUniversity of Ottawa, Canada and University of Luxembourg, Luxembourg\nICSE 2025 GC\nYuanfang Cai\nDrexel University\nICSE 2028 PC\nSilvia Ceballos\nIEEE Computer Society, Los Alamitos, USA\nIEEE CS Conference Business Operations Manager\nNon-voting\nMarsha Chechik\nUniversity of Toronto, Canada\nACM SIGSOFT Chair & ICSE 2018 PC\nMassimiliano Di Penta\nUniversity of Sannio, Italy\nICSE 2023 PC**\nArie van Deursen\nDelft University of Technology, The Netherlands\nICSE Steering Committee Co-Chair and ICSE 2021 PC\nAntonio Filieri\nAmazon Web Services (AWS) and Imperial College London\nICSE 2027 SEIP\nBrian Fitzgerald\nUniversity of Limerick & Lero, Ireland\nICSE 2027 GC\nLars Grunske\nHumboldt-Universität zu Berlin\nICSE 2028 PC\nJohn Grundy\nMonash University, Australia\nICSE 2023 GC**\nHelena Holmström-Olsson\nMalmö University\nICSE 2027 SEIP\nRashina Hoda\nMonash University, Australia\nICSE 2026 SEIP\nCiera Jaspan\nGoogle\nICSE 2025 SEIP\nMarcos Kalinowski\nPontifical Catholic University of Rio de Janeiro, Brazil\nICSE 2026 GC\nRick Kazman\nUniversity of Hawaii, USA\n2nd Past IEEE CS TCSE Chair, ICSE 2025 SEIP, and ICSE 2028 GC\nTim Lethbridge\nUniversity of Ottawa, Canada\nICSE 2025 GC\nQinghua Lu\nCSIRO\nICSE 2028 SEIP\nBrookes Little\nIEEE Computer Society, Los Alamitos, USA\nIEEE CS Senior Manager, Communities & Technical Activities\nNon-voting\nAnna Liu\nAmazon Web Services, Australia\nICSE 2023 SEIP**\nDavid Lo\nSingapore Management University, Singapore\nICSE 2025 PC\nMira Mezini\nTechnische Universität Darmstadt, Germany\nICSE 2026 PC\nNachi Nagappan\nMeta, USA\nICSE 2024 SEIP\nAna C. R. Paiva\nUniversity of Porto, Portugal\nICSE 2024 GC\nCorina Pasareanu\nNASA and CMU, USA\nICSE 2025 PC\nShakira Toomer\nACM, New York, USA\nACM ICSE Meeting Planner\nNon-voting\nGustavo Pinto\nZup Innovation, Brazil\nICSE 2026 SEIP\nRafael Prikladnicki\nPontifical Catholic University of Rio Grande do Sul (PUCRS), Brazil\nICSE 2026 GC\nAbhik Roychoudhury\nNational University of Singapore\nICSE 2024 PC\nFederica Sarro\nUniversity College London, UK\nIEEE CS TCSE Chair\nMargaret-Anne Storey\nUniversity of Victoria, Canada\nICSE Steering Committee Co-Chair and ICSE 2024 PC\nLadan Tahvildari\nUniversity of Waterloo, Canada\n1st Past IEEE CS TCSE Chair\nDongmei Zhang\nMicrosoft Research Asia, China\nICSE 2027 PC\nTom Zimmermann\nUniversity of California, Irvine, USA\n1st Past ACM SIGSOFT Chair & ICSE 2026 PC\nAndrea Zisman\nThe Open University, UK\nICSE 2027 PC\n* — 2nd Past ACM SIGSOFT and IEEE CS TCSE Chairs will rotate off af